<addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO, TAKAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUZUU TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUZUU, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bearing device comprising a bearing (4), a washer (5), a connecting piece (6) formed integral with and connecting the bearing and the washer to each other, and adapted to separate from the bearing (4) and the washer (5) on receiving a pressing force, and a base flap (7) provided with projections (7b). Thus an operator can hold the bearing (4) and the washer (5) as a single component to easily mount them on a shaft (1), and easily separate and remove the connecting piece (6) by means of the projections (7b), so that it is possible to markedly improve a mounting work efficiency and easily cope with automated mounting operations.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif à palier comprenant un palier (4), une rondelle (5), une pièce de raccord (6) intégrée au palier et à la rondelle, reliant les deux et conçue pour se séparer du palier (4) et de la rondelle (5) sous l'effet d'une force de compression, ainsi qu'un volet de base (7) comportant des protubérances (7b). Un opérateur peut donc tenir le palier (4) et la rondelle (5) comme un élément unique pour effectuer aisément le montage de l'ensemble sur un arbre (1). Dès lors, il est facile de séparer et d'extraire la pièce de raccord (6) en utilisant pour cela les protubérances (7b) qu'elle comporte. Il est donc possible d'améliorer considérablement l'efficacité de montage et de s'adapter facilement aux opérations de montage automatisées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>